<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bay of Campeche</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Gulf of Campeche</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bay of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campeche">Campeche</a>, or Gulf of Campeche, is the southern part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-mexico">Gulf of Mexico</a>, bordered by the Mexican states of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/veracruz">Veracruz</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabasco">Tabasco</a> and Campeche. Its offshore fields, above all Cantarell, discovered in the 1970s, made it the centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>'s oil production. It is also an important fishing ground.</p></div>
